# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Yanxiao Hu et al. (2025). Global Universal Scaling and Ultra-Small Parameterization in Machine Learning Interatomic Potentials with Super-Linearity.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2502.07293  arXiv:2502.07293v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2502.07293v1 (sha256 15a8568ca2298dfa...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 194 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the SUS2-MLIP method (introduced here) and eight models
# trained on published or in-house data sets, each with its basis label,
# cutoff and parameter count; energy, force and stress MAEs are encoded
# where the text or SI Table S2 prints them (MPF.2021.2.8, HH130, Cu2-xSe,
# sulfide electrolytes). The benchmark against other architectures is a
# figure. Preprint only (arXiv v1).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

